      "mergedPostDetails": "Fatal error in GC - SuspendThread loop failed only during EAC-protected launch\n\nVRChat intermittently/frequently fails during startup with a Windows dialog:\n\nFatal error in GC\n\nSuspendThread loop failed\n\nThe failure occurs very early during startup, before VRChat finishes loading.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\nStart VRChat normally through Steam.\n\nEasy Anti-Cheat launches normally.\n\nDuring VRChat startup, a \"Fatal error in GC - SuspendThread loop failed\" dialog appears.\n\nVRChat terminates after acknowledging the error.\n\nImportant diagnostic finding:\n\nLaunching VRChat.exe directly without the normal EAC-protected launch consistently starts VRChat successfully in offline testing mode. The SuspendThread failure occurs when launching normally through Steam/Easy Anti-Cheat.\n\nWindows Event Viewer crash information:\n\nFaulting application: VRChat.exe\n\nFaulting module: GameAssembly.dll\n\nException code: 0x80000003\n\nFault offset: 0x0000000000a89d7a\n\nTroubleshooting already performed:\n\nVerified VRChat files through Steam.\n\nRepaired Easy Anti-Cheat.\n\nPerformed EasyAntiCheat_EOS.exe qa-factory-reset.\n\nEAC was successfully reset; Windows requested EAC permissions again afterward.\n\nProblem remained after EAC reset and reboot.\n\nUpdated AMD chipset drivers.\n\nTested with Windows Memory Integrity/HVCI disabled.\n\nTested Windows Defender Real-time Protection both enabled and after toggling it.\n\nTested clean boot / disabling non-Microsoft startup services.\n\nTested with Virtual Desktop, Wacom, Everything and other background services stopped.\n\nNo custom VRChat CPU affinity or Process Lasso configuration is being used.\n\nDirect non-EAC VRChat launch continues to work.",
