      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Still hitting this consistently on a completely fresh reinstall as of today (2026-09-25). Timeline of everything I've tried:\n\n- Disabled Windows Memory Integrity (HVCI) - fixed it for about 2 weeks, then the crash came back on 2026-09-25 without me re-enabling it\n\n- Removed old leftover AMD GPU drivers (ghost devices, Code 45)\n\n- Updated/clean-reinstalled NVIDIA driver (currently 617.14)\n\n- Fully uninstalled SteelSeries GG and its HID driver\n\n- Disabled all overlays (Discord, GeForce overlay, Xbox Game Bar)\n\n- Verified game files via Steam\n\n- Cleared VRChat's local cache folder completely\n\n- Fresh reinstall of VRChat today\n\n- Enabled Windows Defender \"Periodic scanning\" alongside Bitdefender (saw this suggested elsewhere in this thread) - no effect\n\nNone of the above fixed it. Attaching my latest output_log - as expected it cuts off right after basic Steam/localization init, before any content loading, which matches what's described here about the crash happening inside EAC's protected launch before VRChat's own logging can capture anything.\n\nSystem: NVIDIA RTX 5070 Ti (driver 617.14), Windows 11, Bitdefender as primary AV (Windows Defender in passive/periodic mode).\n\nHappy to run any additional diagnostics or provide more logs if it helps narrow this down.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
